Assistant (5) 2026-10-15 09:36:20.988 UTC (+282.6s)

V3.5 completed the lap in 1:42.592 with 0 damage. The closest call to damage was Turn 11 at about 3287 m, so I changed  
V_CORNER_MIN from 55.0 to 50.0 for V3.6. I haven't run V3.6, so I make no lap-time claim for it. The selftest passed,   
and V_CORNER_MIN and the new changelog entry are the only files changed.                                                
                                                                                                                        
V3.5 result                                                                                                             
                                                                                                                        
- Lap time: 1:42.592, which is 4.514 s faster than V3.4 (1:47.106).                                                     
- Damage: 0.0, with 0 offtrack events.                                                                                  
- Max speed: 203.0 km/h at 1769.6 m.                                                                                    
- Time gain: 33 of the 37 100 m bins each gained 0.08–0.20 s over V3.4. The tight-corner bins did not gain: 2400–2500 m 
  lost 0.02 s, 2500–2600 m lost 0.07 s, and 3300–3400 m lost 0.09 s.                                                    
                                                                                                                        
Closest call to damage                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                        
The track half-width in metres isn't logged, so margins are in trackPos units only.                                     
                                                                                                                        
Observations (from ticks.csv):                                                                                          
- Turn 11, 3200–3300 m: peak |trackPos| is 0.891 at 3287.1 m, a margin of 0.109 to the edge (V3.4 peaked at 0.813).     
  Speed there is 61.5 km/h.                                                                                             
- Steering and visibility: steer is at 1.0 for 72 ticks and track9 falls to 5.1 m. There are 29 ticks with |trackPos| > 
  0.8, against 9 in V3.4. This 100 m bin took 4.22 s, the slowest bin on the lap apart from the standing start.         
- Entry versus apex: entry speed at 3180 m rose to 157.2 km/h from 145.0, but the minimum speed barely changed (61.1 vs 
  62.7 km/h). Brake over the entry stretch stayed light (mean 0.16, max 0.24). Throttle stayed at 0.10–0.26 from 3260 m 
  to the apex.                                                                                                          
- Hairpin near 2468 m: peak |trackPos| is 0.740 at 2480 m (V3.4: 0.566), with minimum speed 66.9 km/h and track9 down to
  11.2 m. It stayed under the 0.85 revert threshold from the V3.5 entry.                                                
- Heaviest braking is not at the hairpin. Only 2 ticks have brake ≥ 0.5, at 2231–2232 m (194 km/h, brake 1.0), about 237
  m before the hairpin.                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                        
Hypotheses (not measured):                                                                                              
- The higher BRAKE_DECEL makes the car arrive faster at the tight corners, and that is what widens the line. The log has
  no lateral acceleration or slip, so I can't confirm this.                                                             
- Throttle while the steering is saturated may be taking grip away from turning.                                        
                                                                                                                        
Change applied                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
PARAMS["V_CORNER_MIN"] goes from 55.0 to 50.0.                                                                          
- Expected effect: at Turn 11 with track9 at 13.7 m, the model's target speed drops from 77.7 to 74.3 km/h. This assumes
  the side rays read short (openness 0), which the log can't confirm. At about 76 km/h the car would then brake lightly 
  instead of applying 0.19 throttle. I expect a slightly lower apex speed and a Turn 11 peak |trackPos| below 0.891. The
  cost is 0.05–0.15 s per tight corner, which is an estimate.                                                           
- Risk: low. Revert to 55.0 if there is any damage, or if the lap is slower than 1:42.592 and the Turn 11 peak          
  |trackPos| is still 0.85 or higher.                                                                                   
- I chose this over STEER_SMOOTH because steering is already saturated at both corners, so it can't add correction      
  there. I chose it over BRAKE_DECEL because braking isn't what limits speed at the apex.                               
                                                                                                                        
